Disable SLP vectorization of copyable elements before running the LLVM optimization pipeline.
Vectorizing copyable elements (lanes filled with an idempotent `add x, 0` / `lshr x, 0`)
produces packed PTX that ptxas 12.8.93 miscompiles on sm_90 / sm_100, giving wrong results e.g. in
test_comprehensive_nn_functional_max_pool2d_cuda_float32 (not reproduced on sm_80).
See https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/165691 and https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/167339
Setting DISABLE_LLVM_OPT=slp-copyable-elements re-enables the vectorization.

Backport of https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/9035 (commit 9844da955a9d) which is part of
the v3.6.0 release but not of commit 8fedd49bbfc4 pinned by PyTorch 2.10.0.

diff --git a/python/src/llvm.cc b/python/src/llvm.cc
